# Default rules (permanent)

These apply to **every** project. Do **not** delete, disable, or “skip for this feature.”

| Default | File | Locked behavior |
|---------|------|-----------------|
| Install intake | `install.mdc` | Ask + fill Profile before building |
| Restrictions | `restrictions.mdc` | Secrets, authz, no `.sql`, etc. |
| Forms UI | `forms.mdc` | Unified **custom** form controls |
| UI styling | `ui-styling.mdc` | Shared tokens / customized chrome |
| Validation | `validation.mdc` | Client + server validation |
| DB engine | `database.mdc` | PHP migrate/seed only; prepared statements |
| Phases | `implementation-phases.mdc` | P0–P4 + subs + exit gates |

## Concept-driven (filled at install — not locked content)

| Area | File | How it is set |
|------|------|----------------|
| Business / domain rules | `concept-domain.mdc` | From product **concept** + features |
| Schema / entities | same + migrations | From **concept** (tables follow domain) |
| SEO on/off | Profile + `seo.mdc` | From intake |
| Advanced packs | `*-advanced.mdc` | From rule level choice |

## Never

- Remove or weaken forms / custom styling / validation defaults
- Invent domain tables that ignore the stated concept
- Treat advanced packs as a reason to drop defaults
- Mix or skip implementation phases / exit gates
